// The Cinder Bath Debate (bible 8.2): Kettil and a Guild surveyor argue with real numbers; both are right about
// different things. Surveyor Lorne, crane, a careful man who believes his arithmetic. Runa sings his numbers
// back as a roll-call and they stop being his. Baths_2.

title: Baths_Kettil_Debate
---
<<if has_flag("emberdown.debate.heard")>>
    Kettil: The crane's still doing sums in the steam. Let him. Warm water's free. #still #line:05cc295
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Lorne: Six hundred and twelve residents. Fade at the southern edge: one wingspan a year, rising. #line:06dfe12
Lorne: Anchoring costs four hundred crowns a street. Kettil's Rest has fourteen streets. The Guild will lend it. #line:00681ed
Kettil: And in forty years the same six hundred and twelve. Not one more. Not one hatched. She spits. #plant:5.1 #line:027a1fd
Lorne: Not one fewer, either. Merrow's End had nine hundred. Ask it how many it has now. #line:0a99f53
Kettil: We hold ours by walking it. Every night. Nobody's gone missing on my count. #line:0f9daf3
Lorne: Nobody has gone missing on your count because it has never been tested. Hollowvein tested it. #line:0d26bc1
<<jump Baths_Runa_Debate>>
===

title: Baths_Runa_Debate
---
Runa: Six hundred and twelve. He's right. #line:0349905
Runa: Six hundred and twelve, Kettil's Rest, one. Now sing them. Every one has a name. #line:0f066d3
Lorne: That is not how numbers work. #line:0f562a7
Runa: It's how ours work. Yours stay the same. Ours go up with every chick, and down with every burial. #line:0a07011
-> You're both right. About different things. #line:0fa6ad1
    Lorne: That is the least satisfying thing anyone has said to me this year. #line:0f1b3fa
    Kettil: Ha. Means it's true. #line:0499ef6
    <<flag emberdown.debate.sided 3>>
-> Your numbers never move, Lorne. #line:0fc9830
    Lorne: Anchored ones do not. That is rather the point. I begin to see why it bothers you. #line:05edabc
    <<flag emberdown.debate.sided 1>>
-> Merrow's End loses a song a season. #line:07f5e12
    Kettil: Aye. And it never had a roll-call. We'll see if one can be taught. #line:009df98
    <<flag emberdown.debate.sided 2>>
<<flag emberdown.debate.heard 1>>
===
